.TH HTTP_CANREAD 3
.SH NAME
http_canread \- process readable HTTP socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "ssize_t http_canread(http* " h ", void (*" wantread ")(fd_type), void (*" wantwrite ")(fd_type));"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_canread ()
handles data available for reading on the HTTP client socket
.IR h .
It performs TLS handshake (if enabled), sends the request if not already sent,
and parses incoming response headers and body data.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes read, or -1 on error.